@tradition sunday-story
// The Sunday story (FX14, 0.92.5 item 16; SW1's pitch): a bedtime story for grown-ups. After his last round of the decks
// on Sunday, Chief Holt reads one chapter of a long adventure book in the junior common room, doing the voices, badly.
// Behind WEEKEND_ON. The chapters themselves are a writing job (SW1): a few to start.
k: 464
title: The Sunday story
when: weekly sunday
at: 22:15-22:55
min: 25
jitter: 5
where: 4 pool common-room
hold: 1
who: holt always, night-owl 50%, juniors 45%, common-room 40%, everyone 8%
anim: holt read, everyone none
host: holt
from: holt

== mail
- The Sunday story tomorrow at {time}, the junior common room. Be on time. I don't recap.

== ask
- Holt's reading tonight. He does the voices. Don't tell him I said that.   #funny
- Sunday story at quarter past ten. Grab a beanbag early, they go fast.
- Holt stopped on a cliffhanger last time. I need to know what happens.   #funny

== here
- Shh. He's doing the old pilot's voice.   #funny
- One more page. Please. Just one.   #funny
- Nobody breathe. This is the good bit.

== thanks
- You find a spot on the common room floor. Chief Holt opens the book, clears his throat and reads, doing every voice, badly, while nobody so much as fidgets.

== chatter
- Holt ended the Sunday story on a cliffhanger again. He does it on purpose.   #funny
- I don't go for Holt's voices. I go for Holt's voices.   #funny
- The Sunday story's the only thing that gets the junior wing to bed on time.   #funny
